<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-040-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Dürer/Camper facial grids — whole-grid deformation test on human profile landmarks (Pass 1) — Code-to-model traceability: 70/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Every transformation function names its equation id and Thompson page; the Lean theorems cite the Python functions they mirror; the KG yaml links law -> theorem -> code locus. Deductions: landmark-detection heuristics (prominence 2 % / 0.3 %, 2x rule for li) are not traceable to a published protocol beyond a method-family citation." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "thompson/claims/t1917-040_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py L296–L378: detect_landmarks thresholds are heuristic <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/7d216d80/thompson/claims/t1917-040_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py#L296-L378>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-040-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-040-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 7e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-040-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Dürer/Camper facial grids — whole-grid deformation test on human profile landmarks (Pass 1) — Model fidelity to source: 66/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "E1/E3/E4/E5 are coded exactly as Thompson states them (x1, c*y1; x = xi - eta cot w, y = eta cosec w; affine X' = AX + t; tan additivity) and the Lean module proves the group law, whole-grid property, facial-angle monotonicity, circle->ellipse, affine closure and invertibility with no placeholder. Deductions: the full 6-dof affine fitted to 8-9 nearly collinear landmarks is not Thompson's 2-parameter Dürer grid (stretch c + shear k) and is ill-conditioned — fitted anisotropy ranges 0.11-6.8 and rotation up to 69 deg, which no Dürer head exhibits; type (2) logarithmic stretch (E2) is not implemented." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-040/t1917_040_pairwise_fits.csv (generated output, not in repo): affine_anisotropy 0.11-6.8, affine_rotation_deg up to 69.4, affine_k up to 8.4: ill-conditioned fits — datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-040/t1917_040_pairwise_fits.csv: rendered output of thompson/claims/t1917-040_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py at 7d216d80, text/csv, 1830 B, artifact_sha256 5bd7764c20a22891664d40fd7fbd26bb30b4f69aa118bede1e1282570d15d921 (sha256 5bd7764c20a22891664d40fd7fbd26bb30b4f69aa118bede1e1282570d15d921), spec_fingerprint bf2c0ad03b62d78daf7290b9c4b6a8298b657d4806b6d9a98874151b2165a166",
        "thompson/claims/t1917-040_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py L166–L184: fit_affine is unconstrained 6-dof; no Dürer (c, k) sub-family fit <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/7d216d80/thompson/claims/t1917-040_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py#L166-L184>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-040-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-040-model-fidelity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 6.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-040-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Dürer/Camper facial grids — whole-grid deformation test on human profile landmarks (Pass 1) — Morphometric validation: 42/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Landmark RMSE in centroid-size units for similarity vs affine on every ordered pair, R_affine as the claim statistic, and convexity / nasolabial angles compared with Legan & Burstone norms are computed. Deductions: n = 4 specimens / 12 pairs; no landmark noise floor, so a residual of 0.10 cannot be judged; no leave-one-out CV for a 6-dof fit on 8 points; no negative or positive control on real data; nasolabial SD of 39 deg signals a columella misdetection; convexity computed on only 2 faces." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "thompson/claims/t1917-040_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py L711–L720: verdict_from thresholds on R_affine alone, without noise floor or CV <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/7d216d80/thompson/claims/t1917-040_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py#L711-L720>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-040-measurement-accepted-specimens-with-11-profile-landmarks>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-040-measurement-facial-convexity-angle-g-sn-pg-mean-over-specimens>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-040-measurement-median-landmark-rmse-similarity-null>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-040-measurement-median-landmark-rmse-whole-grid-affine-d-rer-grid>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-040-measurement-median-r-affine-1-ss-affine-ss-similarity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-040-measurement-nasolabial-angle-cm-sn-ls-mean-over-specimens>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-040-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-040-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 4.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-040-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Dürer/Camper facial grids — whole-grid deformation test on human profile landmarks (Pass 1) — MorphoEval overall 53.5/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Thompson's types (1) stretch, (3) shear and their affine closure are implemented exactly and mirrored by 6 Lean theorems. Nine CC/PD profile photographs (SHA-256 pinned) are segmented by a Lab background model and landmarked by the extremum sequence; 4 pass QC (Romy Schneider, Roberts, Odúnóku, Margaret of Hesse), 5 fail (gradient wall shadow, halftone/low contrast, faded lower face, textured background, lettering). On 12 ordered pairs the median landmark RMSE falls from 0.189 (similarity) to 0.103 (affine), median R_affine 0.58 (range 0.04-0.81). Convexity 8.5 deg (n=2, norm 12+/-4), nasolabial 93 deg (n=4, SD 39 — columella misdetected on at least two faces). Provisional verdict \"mixed\"; no noise floor, no CV, no controls. Overall 53.5/100 (faithfulness 46.1, reproducibility 70.9); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 7d216d80; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 66, Morphological realism / specimen match 35, Parameter expressivity 40, Morphometric validation 42, Source and data traceability 80, Code-to-model traceability 70, Reproducibility package 64. Output judged: docs/media/t1917_040_on_the_theory_of_transformatio_comparison.png: rendered output of thompson/claims/t1917-040_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py at 7d216d80, image/png, 516848 B, 1760×1100 px, artifact_sha256 b4e443ab9874866b566b81cbbab7908412d2bcc08e4ac1d3a5d54d94662bd284 (sha256 b4e443ab9874866b566b81cbbab7908412d2bcc08e4ac1d3a5d54d94662bd284), spec_fingerprint bf2c0ad03b62d78daf7290b9c4b6a8298b657d4806b6d9a98874151b2165a166. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: bf2c0ad03b62d78daf7290b9c4b6a8298b657d4806b6d9a98874151b2165a166; artifact_sha256: b4e443ab9874866b566b81cbbab7908412d2bcc08e4ac1d3a5d54d94662bd284; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-040/paper_citations.bib=1279402c7d3411df..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-040/scout_manifest.json=c738aa8c422f8f96..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-040/specimens/beverly_sills_profile.jpg=679a08ff1f459089..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-040/specimens/helen_keller_1904_profile.jpg=7fa2a48b647c3b09..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-040/specimens/kubra_gumusay_2023_profile.jpg=aaa06c6f5c336da7..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-040/specimens/margaret_of_hesse_profile.jpg=1b38e84fc0eb1594..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-040/specimens/nasta_rojc_profile.jpg=4b5ed492fb19ec93..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-040/specimens/nell_walden_1905_profile.png=b1f49c57c7aeefee..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-040/specimens/roberts_2013_profile.jpg=643f14a150df84e0..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-040/specimens/romy_schneider_profile.jpg=0857743562b65c3a..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-040/specimens/winifred_odunoku_profile.jpg=b48ece4b38e69468..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-040/t1917_040_on_the_theory_of_transformatio_reference.json=a4d2db858ac2cfd9..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-040/thompson_1917_pages/ongrowthform1917thom_leaf759_p740.jpg=9e583cdcbd5c7ced..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-040/thompson_1917_pages/ongrowthform1917thom_leaf761_p742.jpg=214db8a09bd3fdfe...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Dürer heads redrawn in rectangular (Fig. 364) and oblique (Fig. 366) nets | Camper's facial angle 'is the index to a general deformation' (p. 742 footnote); no measurements in the source; reconstructed_in_script: E1 stretch, E3 shear with k = -cot(omega), E4 affine, E5 tan(phi') = tan(phi) + k | similarity-vs-affine landmark fits on 4 accepted photographs (12 ordered pairs); transfer_boundary: 2-D soft-tissue silhouettes from photographs, not skulls or 3-D form | forehead often hidden by hair (g/n missing); does_not_claim: anything about populations or 'types' | growth or developmental mechanism." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Independent second assessor (different provider) — this round is builder-scored'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': \"Replace the unconstrained 6-dof affine by Thompson's Dürer sub-family (uniform scale + stretch c + shear k, 5 dof, fitted in the Procrustes frame) so the parameters are interpretable and the fit is conditioned on nearly collinear profile landmarks; keep the affine as an upper bound\"}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Add dense arc-length semilandmarks of the profile curve between the top landmark and menton so the fit is not driven by 8 points'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Noise floor: re-detect landmarks under image perturbation (rescale 0.85/1.15, blur 1 px) and report RMSE; LOO-CV residual for every pair'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R5', 'item': 'Controls on real data: positive (exact Dürer grid applied to a specimen is recovered), negative (scrambled correspondences), ablation (local nose-only displacement is NOT absorbed by the grid)'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R6', 'item': 'Statistical goodness of fit: Pearson r and RMSE of fitted k vs measured facial-line tan change (E5), KS test similarity vs affine residuals, CV of R across pairs'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R7', 'item': \"Parameter-regime sweep over omega (50-130 deg) and c (0.67-1.5) applied to a real specimen with angle read-outs; digitise the obliquity of Thompson's Fig. 366 nets from the pinned scan (Hough transform)\"}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R8', 'item': 'Segmentation: rescue the gradient-background specimen (edge-assisted refinement) and fix the columella / nasion detection that produce a 39 deg nasolabial SD and a nasion on the hair fringe; pick the GIF specimen with a visible forehead'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 5.35e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-040-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Dürer/Camper facial grids — whole-grid deformation test on human profile landmarks (Pass 1) — Parameter expressivity: 40/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The animation sweeps Thompson's omega 60->120 deg and shows the facial line tilting monotonically with k (E5), and the self-test proves the affine recovers an exact Dürer grid. But the analysis itself has no parameter sweep (c, k, eps), the fitted affine parameters are not interpretable because of the conditioning problem, and nothing demonstrates what range of (c, k) real faces occupy." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
